{"clientPlatform": "android", "cwd": "/home/user/rainbow-", "entrypoint": "remote_mobile", "gitBranch": "ccr-6f431adf-7h0m8y", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": "@\"/root/.claude/uploads/515c677b-ab06-5e2e-a8b1-8f1fec6cb7a1/0262b784-Rainbow_11_Screen_Claude_Code_Kit.zip\" @\"/root/.claude/uploads/515c677b-ab06-5e2e-a8b1-8f1fec6cb7a1/f9160ba8-Rainbow_Claude_Code_Master_Prompt_11_Screens.md\" START NEW PROJECT — RAINBOW\n\nFull 11-Screen 3D Mobile Game\n\nClaude, I am starting a BRAND-NEW GAME called RAINBOW.\n\nThis is a completely separate game project. Do not reuse repositories, branches, characters, code, or 3D assets from any of my previous games.\n\nCreate a new isolated project and, when authorized, a new private GitHub repository named \"rainbow-washer-game\".\n\nI have provided my full Rainbow reference package containing 11 approved game screens and one official cartoon girl reference.\n\nIMPORTANT: Read \"Rainbow_Claude_Code_Master_Prompt_11_Screens.md\", \"REFERENCE_ORDER.md\", \"CLAUDE.md\", and inspect every uploaded image at full resolution before beginning. Follow the complete master prompt.\n\n1. BUILD MY EXACT APPROVED SCREENS\n\nI want a beautiful, premium-quality, real-time 3D mobile game that looks as close as technically possible to my original screenshots.\n\nThe screens must remain in this exact order:\n\n1. 01 — Inside the Washing Machine: The official cartoon girl walks away. Benny is concealed in the purple towel inside the washer.\n2. 02 — Whirlpool Tumble: Benny spins with the clothing in the colorful detergent water.\n3. 03 — Whirlpool Twirl: Benny spins toward the glowing drain and blue slide.\n4. 04 — Through the Five Arrows: Benny travels down the steep blue water slide with five glowing white arrows.\n5. 05 — Flow Into the Current: Benny enters the winding blue-and-pink washer current.\n6. 06 — Crest the Rinse Arch: The water carries him over the dramatic curved arch.\n7. 07 — Dive the Washer Tube: Benny follows the winding tube, then descends very deep into the washing machine.\n8. 08 — Final Spin Chamber: The bottom of that deep descent physically connects into the final chamber.\n9. 09 — Ride the Final Wave: Benny rides the large wave through that same chamber.\n10. 10 — Slide Into Hiding: Benny slides beneath the purple towel, away from the girl's sight.\n11. 11 — Safely Home: The official cartoon girl opens the washer door and holds the purple towel. Benny remains safely concealed. Display the final victory message, FINAL SPIN COMPLETE.\n\nScreen 11 is the real ending. There must be no additional stage after it.\n\n2. THE OFFICIAL CARTOON GIRL\n\nUse the uploaded \"official_cartoon_girl_original.jpg\" reference as the official girl for this game.\n\nShe must have:\n\n- Curly brown ponytail.\n- Purple bow headband with yellow star.\n- Large expressive cartoon eyes and a friendly face.\n- Gold hoop earrings.\n- Purple-and-white striped hoodie with yellow star detail.\n- Blue jeans with yellow star patch.\n- Purple-and-white sneakers with yellow star details.\n\nCreate ONE reusable 3D girl model and rig.\n\nUse that exact same girl at the opening, wherever she is visible near the end, and in Screen 11.\n\nThe older girl in the final approved screenshot is a composition reference only. Replace her appearance with my new cartoon girl.\n\nPreserve the final image's camera angle, washer interior, metallic door, platform, towel, lighting and victory banner.\n\nDo not replace the cartoon girl with a realistic woman. Do not create a different girl for the ending.\n\nHer appearance must match Benny's polished, cute 3D game-world style.\n\n3. BENNY MUST NEVER CHANGE\n\nUse the exact Benny character from my approved pictures:\n\nPink fluffy round body, big violet eyes, pink paw pads, purple-and-white striped knitted hat, oversized purple pom-pom and gold star.\n\nOne consistent 3D model and one reusable character rig throughout the game.\n\nHis animations must include swimming, paddling, tumbling, turning, sliding and reacting to the water.\n\n4. EXACT WATER AND WASHING-MACHINE SCENERY\n\nThe environments must reproduce the approved screenshots, including:\n\n- Bright luminous electric-cyan and hot-pink flowing water.\n- Thick rolling water waves and strong glossy highlights.\n- White foam along the water edges.\n- Hundreds of appropriately scaled tiny bubbles and larger iridescent floating bubbles.\n- Shiny magenta-purple perforated washing-machine drum walls.\n- Thick metallic gold tunnel rings and machinery.\n- Gold dollar tokens following the water path.\n- Correct camera placement, depth, character sizing and glowing lighting.\n\nCreate real 3D environment geometry, not flat screenshots.\n\nThe water must actually move, and Benny must move naturally with it.\n\n5. SCREEN 07 MUST CONNECT PERFECTLY TO SCREEN 08\n\nThis is one of my biggest priorities.\n\nAfter the visible stretch of Screen 07, the tube must curve downward into a long, dramatic plunge.\n\nBenny must travel all the way down to a much lower elevation.\n\nAt the bottom, the same tube and flowing water must lead directly into Screen 08's Final Spin Chamber.\n\nNo teleporting. No abrupt scene jump. No disappearing tunnel. No unexplained change of elevation.\n\nThe camera follows Benny throughout the entire descent.\n\nProvide separate proof screenshots showing the beginning, middle, bottom and connection into Screen 08.\n\n6. USE THE BEST 3D AND TESTING TOOLS\n\nInvestigate, connect and verify:\n\nBlender MCP for precise 3D modeling of tunnels, metallic rings, washer mechanisms, doors, platforms, characters and scenery.\n\nMeshy MCP for creating individual 3D assets, including the new cartoon girl, Benny's model, clothing and props. Correct all generated assets in Blender.\n\nHyper3D Rodin MCP as an optional alternative for difficult 3D assets.\n\nWorld Labs Marble/Atlas as an optional environmental modeling and reference tool. Verify the actual available integration before using it.\n\nPlaywright MCP to capture actual running gameplay screens at mobile resolutions, compare them against the approved images, and test movement and controls.\n\nUse verified, documented tool installations. Do not claim a plugin is connected unless tested. Ask before spending paid generation credits.\n\n7. CREATE THESE TEN SPECIALISTS\n\nUse the provided \".claude/agents/\" files:\n\n1. Reference Match Director\n2. Benny Character Artist\n3. Cartoon Girl Character Artist\n4. Washer Environment Modeler\n5. Water FX Specialist\n6. Foam and Bubble Specialist\n7. Path and Camera Transition Engineer\n8. Animation and Gameplay Engineer\n9. Playwright Visual QA Specialist\n10. Android Build and Performance Specialist\n\nThe Water FX Specialist is especially important.\n\nThat specialist must create high-quality animated water shaders, flowing water geometry, wave crests, foam, bubbles, reflections and splashes that closely reproduce my approved artwork while performing well on Android.\n\nThese are custom Claude Code specialists, not imaginary third-party plugins.\n\n8. REAL MOBILE GAMEPLAY\n\nUse Three.js, TypeScript, Blender-exported GLB models and an Android-capable packaging system such as Capacitor.\n\nI need:\n\n- Playable third-person 3D movement.\n- Fast but controllable swimming and sliding.\n- Smooth camera turns and tilts.\n- Real coin collection.\n- Hearts, counters, level titles and pause.\n- Responsive portrait mobile rendering.\n- Natural human animation during the opening and ending.\n- The exact 11-scene sequence.\n\nThe girl must never discover Benny inside the purple towel.\n\n9. AUTOMATIC VISUAL MATCHING\n\nUse Playwright to render each scene from the actual running game.\n\nCreate screenshots numbered 01 through 11.\n\nCompare each scene with its matching uploaded reference using side-by-side comparisons and transparent overlays.\n\nCorrect differences in geometry, character appearance, water color, reflections, bubbles, camera position, lighting, HUD and composition.\n\nFor the first and final images, remember that the new cartoon girl is an intentional character replacement.\n\nTarget approximately 90–95% visual fidelity or better wherever feasible, but disclose real differences rather than claiming an unverified perfect match.\n\nDo not stop after producing screenshots. The environments must be fully playable 3D.\n\n10. SAVE AND VERIFY EVERYTHING\n\nBuild this in the new Rainbow project only.\n\nKeep the original images unchanged.\n\nCommit completed milestones to the new private GitHub repository. Show me the actual repository URL, branch and pushed commit SHA.\n\nIf GitHub access or a required tool connection is unavailable, report the blocker accurately and continue local development where possible.\n\nGive me all eleven actual game screenshots individually and in order, rather than one collage.\n\nSTART NOW: Read the full master prompt and inspect the original files, verify your tools, set up the specialists, and begin implementing the real 3D Rainbow game.\n\nDo not deliver only another plan. Begin creating the playable project.", "role": "user"}, "origin": {"kind": "human"}, "parentUuid": "de91df66-37fe-44d6-85f0-589f2418e6f6", "permissionMode": "default", "promptId": "684dfd2d-1ccc-4357-b4b4-e44e4f078bcd", "promptSource": "sdk", "savedFiles": [{"file_uuid": "0262b784-a5c8-4fa4-8f4f-edec0b5269fa", "inlined": false, "path": "/root/.claude/uploads/515c677b-ab06-5e2e-a8b1-8f1fec6cb7a1/0262b784-Rainbow_11_Screen_Claude_Code_Kit.zip"}, {"file_uuid": "f9160ba8-1a66-4e74-8a66-fd643f2a6901", "inlined": false, "path": "/root/.claude/uploads/515c677b-ab06-5e2e-a8b1-8f1fec6cb7a1/f9160ba8-Rainbow_Claude_Code_Master_Prompt_11_Screens.md"}], "sessionId": "515c677b-ab06-5e2e-a8b1-8f1fec6cb7a1", "timestamp": "2026-11-15T16:32:35.096Z", "turnAttributionKey": "6bd86e01-8f25-4a13-a4b9-e238f181c9b4", "turnOrigin": "human", "turnPosition": {"promptIndex": 1, "turnIndex": 1}, "type": "user", "userType": "external", "uuid": "6bd86e0